course: dictionary
lesson: 15645
title: Thatcher: a job and a name
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A thatcher is a worker who makes roofs. Look at the clue in this sentence: «The thatcher spent three weeks covering the cottage roof with straw.» Spent and covering tell you the thatcher is doing a job, so the word names a person.
explain: Thatchers use straw, reeds or other dry plants. A roof made this way is called a thatched roof. «The thatched roof kept the rain out for years.» The word thatched is a clue that the roof is made from these dry plants.
explain: Look at the capital letter in Thatcher. Names of people always start with a capital letter. Margaret Thatcher was a Prime Minister, so the name here belongs to a person in history. When you see a capital letter in the middle of a sentence, ask: is this a name?
fact: A thatcher is a person whose job is to make roofs from straw, reeds or similar dry plants.
fact: «Thatched» means covered with a roof made of straw or reeds.
fact: Thatching is an old craft still used on cottages in England and Ireland.
fact: Thatcher with a capital T is a surname, a family name.
fact: Margaret Thatcher was Prime Minister of the United Kingdom from 1979 to 1990, the first woman in that job.
exercise: «The thatcher worked high on the cottage roof, laying straw.» What is a thatcher? | A person who cuts hair | A kind of tall tree | *A person who makes roofs from straw or reeds | A type of bread
exercise: The word «Thatcher» starts with a capital T. What kind of word is it? | A verb meaning to run | A kind of weather | A colour | *A name, such as a surname
exercise: «The cottage had a thatched roof made of reeds.» Find and copy the word that tells you what the roof was made from. | *Reeds | Had | Cottage | Roof
test: «Margaret Thatcher was the first woman Prime Minister of the United Kingdom.» What do we learn from this? | She wrote the dictionary | She was a thatcher who made roofs | She was a farmer in Ireland | *She was a Prime Minister, the first woman in that job
test: Which job uses straw and reeds to build roofs? | Glazier | Plumber | *Thatcher | Baker
exam: Which sentence uses thatcher as a job, not as a name? | Thatcher is a long word | Margaret Thatcher spoke in the hall | The Thatcher family moved to the village | *The thatcher re-covered the barn with fresh reeds
